I enjoy browsing through the code to find out how things work.  I find
nethack interesting even when I know exactly how it works (and, of
course, the code is so cryptic, I never will know exactly).

Anyways, for those of you who want to try eating various corpses to
see what intrinsics you get, don't read this, it'll just spoil your fun.

<SPOILERS>












[anyone know how to get a ^L in the default editor for xrn?]










Here are the chances of getting intrisic poison resistance from all
non-poisonous monsters.  The chance is (monster leve)/15 * (chance of
not getting another intrisic instead).  Surprisingly, these chances 
don't depend on what intrinsics you currently have.

This list is complete and accurate, aside from all the unintentional
omissions and mistakes. :-)

Level   Chance of getting   Monster
10          66.6%           golden naga
8           53.3%           black naga
5           33.3%           quivering blob
4           26.6%           all unicorns
6           24.0%           red naga
5           22.2%           brown pudding
10          22.2%           black pudding
3           20.0%           gray ooze
3           20.0%           violet fungi (hallucination)
3           20.0%           quasit
3        <= 20.0%           all naga hatchlings
4           19.6%           blue jelly
9            9.6%           flesh golem
6            9.6%           tengu
1            6.6%           cave spider
1            6.2%           brown mold
1            6.2%           red mold
+ various other things which don't actually leave corpses

The following are also not poisonous, and have poison resistance, but
for one reason or another, probably aren't worth eating to get poison
resistance.

5  cockatrice (stoning)
11 nurse (human)
30 Wizard of Yendor (only gives intrisic teleportation, human)
1  barbarian (human)
1  healer (human)
6  wraith (cannot convey intrinsics)


